                <pb facs="0484" n="424" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg424"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Mr. Vignaud</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-03-12"><hi rendition="#italic">March 12,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>At the request of the Venezuelan Government you will, with the acquiescence of
                    the Government of France, upon the retirement of Venezuelan minister and upon
                    application by him, afford your friendly good offices for the protection of
                    Venezuelan citizens in France; but you will not represent Venezuela
                    diplomatically, nor will consuls under you act in official representation of
                    Venezuela.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Uhl</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Acting</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
